<http://gcrc.carleton.ca/ontologies/2023/GCRC_CEBP_Genome_Architecture/Species> a owl:Class .
<http://gcrc.carleton.ca/ontologies/2023/GCRC_CEBP_Genome_Architecture/SpeciesGenomicsData>
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf <http://gcrc.carleton.ca/ontologies/2023/GCRC_CEBP_Genome_Architecture/BiogenomeDataAndProcess> ;
  dc:description "The Soecues Genomics Data entity pulls data from the Canada Biogenome project in the form of several specific, constrained metadata fields. This constrained-parameter view is presented as a filter of information to allow users to more easily and quickly understand, for a particular species, if a sample for genomics analysis has been acquired, if the sample has been sequenced, and to view the quality identifier of a genome sequence." ;
  ns0:scientificName "" ;
  ns0:taxonNameID "" ;
  rdfs:label "Species Genomics Data" .

<http://gcrc.carleton.ca/ontologies/2023/GCRC_CEBP_Genome_Architecture/WorkingGroup>
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf <http://gcrc.carleton.ca/ontologies/2023/GCRC_CEBP_Genome_Architecture/Consumers>, [
    a owl:Restriction ;
    owl:onProperty <http://gcrc.carleton.ca/ontologies/2023/GCRC_CEBP_Genome_Architecture/collaborativelyImplements> ;
    owl:someValuesFrom <http://gcrc.carleton.ca/ontologies/2023/GCRC_CEBP_Genome_Architecture/ConservationStrategy>
  ] ;
  dc:description """Working Group Objectives (example):
1. Provide a mechanism for networking and collaboration among
diverse interests in the conservation of a species.
2. Provide a forum to discuss active projects, the latest research, and
co-ordinated approaches to threat mitigation.
3. Provide expert advice, education, and outreach to organizations
and individuals on a species' conservation.
4. Encourage ecosystem-based or other Conservation Strategy or Conservation Action approaches to species
recovery and ensure integration of in situ and ex situ efforts in a
One Plan Approach, or other approach
5. Include a two-eyed seeing approach that incorporates many
knowledge systems to all activities.""" ;
  dc:source "Chabot, A., Thompson, H., Colston, L., Elliott, G., McCurdy-Adams, H., & Maloney, A. 2023. Eastern Massasauga Rattlesnake Genomics Workshop: Participant Handbook. Canadian Species Initiative (CSI), Cambridge, ON, CAN." .

<http://gcrc.carleton.ca/ontologies/2023/GCRC_CEBP_Genome_Architecture/application>
