  ns2:translation "Respecting others, relationships, and caring for people."@en .

<http://gcrc.carleton.ca/ontologies/2023/GCRC_CEBP_Genome_Architecture/Kunming-MontrealGlobalBiodiversityFramework>
  a owl:NamedIndividual, <http://gcrc.carleton.ca/ontologies/2023/GCRC_CEBP_Genome_Architecture/collaborativeConservationFrameworks> ;
  dc:description "The Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework (GBF) is a landmark international agreement adopted in 2022 to halt and reverse biodiversity loss by 2030, aiming for a biodiverse world, living in harmony with human processes, by 2050. The framework set 23 targets for countries to collectively protect ecosystems, including those that safeguard and recognize Indigenous rights and knowledge (Targets 21-22), including Free, Prior, and Informed Consent (FPIC) and the full, equitable, and effective participation of Indigenous peoples in biodiversity-related decision-making at all levels."@en ;
  rdfs:label "Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework (GBF)" .

